/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (In our project, we used Visual Studio Code, a source code editor developed by Microsoft, widely appreciated for its versatility and rich features. This tool allowed us to work efficiently on web development by providing a user-friendly interface, support for many programming languages, debugging features, intelligent autocompletion, and numerous useful extensions created by the community. With Visual Studio Code, we were able to manage our project effectively and produce high-quality code. Additionally, I used Docker to run a PostgreSQL container, enabling an isolated and consistent environment for database management. For working with the database, I used DataGrip, a powerful database management tool. To ensure the API functions correctly, I used Postman for testing the endpoints. Version control was handled through Git and GitHub, enabling seamless collaboration and code management throughout the development process.)
/E (In our project, we used Visual Studio Code, a source code editor developed by Microsoft, widely appreciated for its versatility and rich features. This tool allowed us to work efficiently on web development by providing a user-friendly interface, support for many programming languages, debugging features, intelligent autocompletion, and numerous useful extensions created by the community. With Visual Studio Code, we were able to manage our project effectively and produce high-quality code. Additionally, I used Docker to run a PostgreSQL container, enabling an isolated and consistent environment for database management. For working with the database, I used DataGrip, a powerful database management tool. To ensure the API functions correctly, I used Postman for testing the endpoints. Version control was handled through Git and GitHub, enabling seamless collaboration and code management throughout the development process.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
